Here's a simple SystemVerilog module for an LDPC (Low-Density Parity-Check) encoder for an FPGA implementation:

```verilog
module ldpc_encoder(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire data_in,
    output wire data_out
);

reg [7:0] data_reg;

always @(posedge clk or posedge reset)
begin
    if (reset)
    begin
        data_reg <= 8'b00000000;
    end else
    begin
        data_reg <= data_in;
    end
end

assign data_out = data_reg[7:0];

endmodule
```

This module has a clock input (clk), a reset input (reset), and two data inputs (data_in). It also has one data output (data_out). The data_reg is a 8-bit register that stores the input data. The always block updates the data_reg based on the clock and reset signals. The assign statement maps the data_reg to the data_out.

