Using the UpdateAAD() method in an AEAD GCM cipher class is useful when you want to update the additional authenticated data (AAD) during encryption or decryption operations. To use this method, follow these steps:

1. Create an instance of the AEAD GCM cipher class:
```csharp
using System.Security.Cryptography;

AEAD_GCM gcm = new AEAD_GCM();
```
1. Initialize the cipher with the key and IV:
```csharp
gcm.Key = // your key;
gcm.IV = // your initialization vector;
```
1. Set the AAD that you want to use during encryption or decryption operations:
```csharp
gcm.AdditionalAuthenticationData = "your AAD data";
```
1. Encrypt or decrypt data using the UpdateAAD() method:
```csharp
// Encrypt data
byte[] encryptedBytes = gcm.Encrypt(dataToEncrypt);

// Decrypt data
byte[] decryptedBytes = gcm.Decrypt(encryptedBytes);
```
In the example above, we first set the AAD using the AdditionalAuthenticationData property. Then, we call the Encrypt() or Decrypt() method, which automatically updates the AAD during the operation. This ensures that the same AAD is used throughout the entire encryption or decryption process.

Keep in mind that updating the AAD can affect the security of your data, so make sure to use it appropriately and only when necessary. Additionally, ensure that the AAD is not sensitive information, as it will be included in the encrypted data.

