3. In your `next.config.js` file, import the `cors` middleware and add it to the `middlewares` array:
```javascript
// next.config.js
const cors = require('./pages/cors');

module.exports = {
  // ...
  middlewares: [cors],
};
```
4. Now, when you make API requests from your Next.js app to your WordPress site, the CORS error should be resolved.

Note: Make sure to replace `http://your-wordpress-site.com` with the actual URL of your WordPress site. Also, you may need to adjust the `methods` and `origin` options to suit your specific needs.

