To leverage the Accord.NET library in C# to train and implement the Naive Bayes algorithm for text classification, follow these steps:

1. Install the Accord.NET NuGet package.
2. Load the dataset of labeled sentences into a `List<(string sentence, string category)>`.
3. Create a `NaiveBayes` classifier and fit it on the dataset.
4. Use the `CountVectorizer` class to transform the dataset into a matrix of word counts.
5. Classify a new sentence using the fitted model.

Here's a concise and elegant C# code that accomplishes this task:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Classification;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Features;

public class TextClassification
{
    public static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Load the dataset of labeled sentences
        var dataset = new List<(string sentence, string category)>
        {
            ("The sports game was exciting", "sports"),
            ("The political rally was heated", "politics"),
            ("The entertainment show was amazing", "entertainment"),
            // Add more labeled sentences here
        };

        // Create a Naive Bayes classifier and fit it on the dataset
        var classifier = new NaiveBayes();
        classifier.Fit(dataset.Select(x => x.sentence).ToArray(), dataset.Select(x => x.category).ToArray());

        // Use the CountVectorizer class to transform the dataset into a matrix of word counts
        var vectorizer = new CountVectorizer();
        var transformedDataset = vectorizer.Transform(dataset.Select(x => x.sentence).ToArray());

        // Classify a new sentence using the fitted model
        var newSentence = "The sports game was exciting";
        var prediction = classifier.Predict(transformedDataset[newSentence]);
        Console.WriteLine($"Predicted label: {prediction}");
    }
}
```

Replace the sample sentence with your new sentence to test the classification process. The predicted label will be printed to the console.

